    <td><p align="left"><b><u> Definition of a Raid-</u></b><br>
      1. 12 people must attend a minor or sub raid. 18 people must attend a major raid. No less. If less than the minimum required people are there, no points will be awarded or paid.&nbsp;<br>
      2. A raid MUST be posted on the board. Otherwise, you have people picking favorites. Everyone must be given a chance to sign up<br>
      3. Raids must be coordinated through the Raid Coordinators.  A Raid Captain may be selected by a Raid Coordinator to run the raid in the coordinator's
      absence.<br>
      4. Any number of raids will be allowed per week.<br>
      5. All raids must be approved by the Raid Coordinator.<br>
      -- Major raids- ALL Alter Planes, Dragons, Zone Boss's (Levels 45-60)<br>
      -- Minor raids- (Levels 25-44)<br>
      -- Sub raids - (Levels 15-24)<br>
      6. Number of people per raid:<br>
      -- Minor and sub raids - Min 12, Max is TBD per raid<br>
      -- Major raids - Min 18, Max is TBD per raid<br>
      <br>
      <br>
      <b><u>Earning Points</u></b><br>
      1. Sub raids - can earn raiders a possible 2 points.<br>
      -- +1 point if you are there on time and staying at least one hour<br>
      -- +1 point if you are there after the break, till the end, and stay at least one hour<br>
      -- Staying 2+ hours will automatically grant full raid points regardless of
      break-in or length of stay considerations. (2 points)<br>
      2. Minor raids - can earn raiders a possible 5 points.<br>
      -- +1 point if you are there on time and staying at least one hour<br>
      -- +2 points if you are there after the break and stay for one hour<br>
      -- +2 points if you stay for raid duration....from break to finish.<br>
      -- Staying 4+ hours will automatically grant full raid points regardless of
      break-in or length of stay considerations. (5 points)<br>
      3. Major raids - can earn a possible 10 points. This is because of the length they take to complete.<br>
      -- +2 points for being on time and staying at least two hours<br>
      -- +4 points if you are there after the break and stay for 2 hours<br>
      -- +2 pts if you stay from break to at least half of the raid time.<br>
      -- +2 pts if you stay from break to the end. (this is in addition to the 2 points above)<br>
      -- Staying 6+ hours will automatically grant full raid points regardless of
      break-in or length of stay considerations. (10 points)<br>
      4. Notes:<br>
      -- On raids that are 10 plus hours and such, you are going to have people going LD, or people who have to grab a quick lunch. It is silly to say that if you have to run to the store for 20 minutes, yet you are there the other 10 plus hours, that you wont get the full 10 points. This being so, here is the buffer that was decided on:  Bonus point buffer from being there start to at least half or finish- You MUST be in on the break to start. You may leave the raid no MORE than 30 min before it is completed, and DURING the raid, you can NOT be gone for more than 1 hour total time.  These times will be documented. We compare all of our information before we post the final point totals.&nbsp;<br>
      -- Points can only be earned if you participate in raids suitable for your level.<br>
      -- Points can NOT be transferred between members or between characters.<br>
      <br>
      These rules must be adhered too. People being late, going LD for extended periods of time, leaving for extended periods of time disrupts the tempo of a raid and the overall length of a raid.<br>
      <br>
      <br>
      <br>
      <b><u>How points are spent</u></b><br>
      Points are spent in three ways:<br>
      <br>
      <u>Class armors / Non-god items  / Epic or Armor Quest items</u><br>
      1. Can be claimed by a minimum number of points.  The number of points that must be bid goes up for each item already won.  The 1st bid is 10, 2nd is 20, etc.  More points may be spent to obtain the item, but this must be stated in advance to the Raid Coordinator/Captain.  Since the time involved to loot items is generally short, you will only be allowed 1 tell stating how many points you wish to spend.  Make sure you state how much you wish to spend carefully.  After all players have stated how many points they wish to spend, the Highest bidder will be awarded the item and have that number of points deducted from their totals.  In the case of 2 or more players having matching bids, the Raid Coordinator/Captain will random amongst them.  In the case where only 1 player bid, that player will be allowed to loot the item for the 10 point minimum.  If no one wishes to bid on an item, the item will be randomed amongst those who wish to forfeit points from the raid to obtain them.  If again no one wishes to claim the item and the item is no-drop, the item will be randomed for no cost.  If the item is droppable and no one who can use the item wishes to claim it, the item will be opened up for bids amongst all players present.  The system continues the same as before with this larger group.  To recap:<br>
      -- Players who can use the item place bids with the RC.  Bids must abide by that player's minimum.<br>
      -- High bid wins for cost of the bid amount.  Ties are randomed for bid amount.  A Single bidder wins for the cost of 10 pts.<br>
      -- If item unclaimed and no-drop, random amongst those wishing to forfeit current raid points for it (can only be done once per raid).  If no one wishes to forfeit points for the item, random amongst all users for no cost.<br>
      -- If item unclaimed and not no-drop, all players who wish to bid may do so.  Min bid is still 10 pts.  Repeat system as above (if unclaimed after bid, random to those who wish to forfeit pts.  if unclaimed after that, planar random)<br>
      <br>
      Example 1: Cleric Legs drop in hate. Cleric A (who has 50 points) passes on the item.  Cleric B (who has 49 points) also passes on the item.  Clerics C, D, and E already have legs. Now Cleric A and B can either 1) pass on the item again and not forfeit the points earned for that raid, or 2) Forfeit any points received on the raid to claim the item. Cleric A passes on forfeiting the points. Cleric B also has the same two options. If he too passes, Cleric A and B random the item for no cost.&nbsp;<br>
      Example 2: Cleric Helm drops in hate.  Cleric A (who has 15 points) has already won one item.  Cleric B (who also has 15 points) has not won an item yet.  Cleric A is required to bid a minimum of  20 points, so can't bid.  Cleric B is required to bid a minimum of 10 points, so can bid 10 to 15 for it.<br>
      2. Each person gets one claim per raid for forfeiting points, and one claim per raid for open random.   If everyone competing for an item has used up their one claim in the open random, that claim process starts over.&nbsp;<br>
      Example 1:  Cleric A has forfeited points for a bracer.  Cleric B has forfeited points for gauntlets.  Neither cleric may forfeit points again on this raid.<br>
      Example 2:  Cleric A and B have both won an open random when boots drop.  Both clerics can now open random on this item since they had both already gotten something previously (assuming that the item makes it to open random)<br>
      3. There is no limit on the number of items a player may bid for, assuming that the player has the points to bid and can meet the minimum bid requirement.<br>
      <br>
      <br>
      <u>God / Dragon / Zone Boss Loot</u>&nbsp;<br>
      1. The bidding system is the same as above with the change that the minimum bid is 20 points.<br>
      Example -- Cazic Thule drops a soulleach, SK A does not wish to bid points (he has 80 points total), SK B does not wish to claim for 20 points either (He has 60 points). Now, SK A  and B have a chance to claim by forfeiting  points. If they both pass, since it is NO DROP, they random. This is not counted as their one GOD LOOT CLAIM.&nbsp;<br>
      2. Each person will get one god loot CLAIM until all the other classes that can reasonably use that item have a god/dragon loot, except as noted above.&nbsp;<br>
      3. God loot claims are independent of class/epic items and do not count against those totals.  In the case where the god/dragon loot is also an epic item, it remains classified as a god/dragon loot.<br>
      <br>
      <u>Minor and sub-raid loot</u><br>
      1. The bidding system is the same as above with the changes that the minimum bid is 1 point and never goes up with the number of items won.<br>
      <br>
      <br>
      <b><u>Open issues Q &amp; A</u></b><br>
      1. Q: What if I don't have enough points to claim an item?&nbsp;</p>
      <p align="left"> A: If you do not have enough points to claim an item, you cannot keep someone from claiming their xth item of the raid. For example, Wizard A has 60 points, Carmine Sleeves drop and he wishes to claim.   He bids the minimum (10 pts) and gets the item.  In this case a Carmine Robe drops after the sleeves, the only other Wizard on the raid only has 7 points. Wizard B cannot stop Wizard A from claiming again at 20 points.&nbsp;<br>
      </p>
      <p align="left">2. Q: When do I get my points?&nbsp;</p>
      <p align="left"> A: You will not be given points for the current raid until after the raid is completed. Therefore, if it is your first raid with us, you will not have the opportunity to CLAIM anything except by forfeiting points, if the loot process goes that far. You will however be allowed to random on anything that you can use that goes to random.&nbsp;<br>
      </p>
      <p align="left">3. Q: What if the item is droppable but I don't wish to claim it?&nbsp;</p>
      <p align="left"> A: If it goes to random, and no one wishes to claim the item, it will be taken for our Guild Treasury.&nbsp;<br>
      </p>
      <p align="left">4. Q: Is this loot policy perfect?&nbsp;</p>
      <p align="left"> A: Probably not. Please provide us with feedback on our message board or speak to us in game with your suggestions. We are always looking to improve the process.&nbsp;<br>
      </p>
      <p align="left">5. Q: What do I do with the Jewel Craft and money items?&nbsp;</p>
      <p align="left"> A: The Raid Coordinator, Raid Captain or some other officer will be collecting these items.  These items will be distributed based on the raid fee policy.  In the case of gems that are needed for quests, these items will be offered up for bid as described above.<br>
      </p>
      <p align="left">6. Q: What happens with Plane of Sky items?&nbsp;</p>
      <p align="left"> A: Plane of sky quest items will go through the same process as regular items with the exception that the minimum bid will be 5 points instead of 10.<br>
      </p>
      <p align="left">7. Q: What if I don't know the stats on an item?&nbsp;</p>
      <p align="left"> A: Read up on any items that have a chance to drop that you can use and/or PoS quest items used in your quests. We will not waste time reading the information off over and over again during raids.&nbsp;<br>
      </p>
      <p align="left">8. Q: What if I signed up for a raid and when I get there I don't know who my group leader is?&nbsp;</p>
      <p align="left"> A: We will not spend time announcing the groups unless major changes occur. Before the raid begins you must look at the message board. Once at the raid it is your responsibility to locate your group leader. The Raid Coordinator or Raid Captain will have already spent a considerable amount of time planning and organizing the raid. We feel the least a raider can do is look at the message boards.   Addendum - Group leaders should make sure to notify the raid leader of any absent members from their group, or when group members have left.  They should try to form their groups up based on the posted setup or setup presented to them when they arrived at the raid.  In other words, group leaders know your group.<br>
      </p>
      <p align="left">9. Q: What if the entire raid only take an hour?&nbsp;</p>
      <p align="left"> A: In the event that the raid goes by quickly, full points will be issued for those who attend the entire raid. Points will also be issued at the discretion of the Raid Coordinator/Raid Captain for members who were not present for the entire raid.
      <br>
      <br>
      </p>
